=== Preference Data Summary ===

Prompt 1: Explain what a neural network is....
  Preferred: Response A
  Rejected:  Response B

Prompt 2: What should I do if my Python code raises a KeyError?...
  Preferred: Response A
  Rejected:  Response B

Prompt 3: Is reinforcement learning the same as supervised learning?...
  Preferred: Response A
  Rejected:  Response B

=== Naive Reward Scores (fraction of times preferred) ===

  Response A total wins: 3/3  (naive reward score: 1.00)
  Response B total wins: 0/3  (naive reward score: 0.00)

=== What a real reward model would do ===
  A reward model (RM) is trained on thousands of these (prompt, chosen, rejected) triples.
  It learns to assign a scalar score to any (prompt, response) pair.
  PPO then updates the language model to generate responses the RM scores highly.

=== STUDENT EXERCISE ===
Edit ground_truth_preferred to flip one judgment (e.g., [1, 0, 1])
Then re-run. What does this mean for the training signal the reward model receives?
Which response in pair 2 is actually better? Do you agree with the annotation?
